sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant A as Auctions - PlaceBidCommandHandler
    participant AH as Auctions - FundsLocked / FundsLockRejected handlers
    participant ADB as Auctions tables
    participant AOP as Auctions OutboxProcessor
    participant W as Wallets - FundsLockRequested / BidPlaced / FundsUnlockRequested handlers
    participant WDB as Wallets tables
    participant WOP as Wallets OutboxProcessor

    C->>A: POST /api/auctions/{id}/bid {amount} with a JWT
    A->>ADB: GetAuctionByIdAsync (tracked entity)
    A->>A: Auction.RequestBid: Active, not ended, amount above CurrentPrice, not the seller, not the leader, no pending bid (else 409)
    A->>A: EndsOn += 30 s when less than AntiSnipingWindow remains, PendingBidderId + PendingBidAmount set, new Version
    A->>ADB: UPDATE Auctions + OutboxMessages(FundsLockRequestedEvent) in one SaveChangesAsync
    A-->>C: 200 - the bid is requested, not yet confirmed
    AOP->>W: Publish(FundsLockRequestedEvent) on the next poll
    W->>WDB: WasEventProcessedAsync(EventId)
    W->>W: Wallet.LockFunds(auctionId, amount): new Active row in the FundsLock ledger
    alt funds locked
        W->>WDB: UPDATE Wallets + WalletsFundsLocks + inbox + WalletsOutboxMessages(FundsLockedEvent)
    else InsufficientFunds or LockAlreadyExists
        W->>WDB: inbox + WalletsOutboxMessages(FundsLockRejectedEvent)
    end
    WOP->>AH: Publish(FundsLockedEvent) on the next Wallets poll
    alt auction still Active
        AH->>ADB: Auction.ConfirmPendingBid: bidder becomes leader + OutboxMessages(BidPlacedEvent) + inbox
    else auction no longer Active
        AH->>ADB: Auction.RejectPendingBid + OutboxMessages(FundsUnlockRequestedEvent) + inbox
    end
    AOP->>W: Publish(BidPlacedEvent): ReleaseLock on the previous leader, amount from the ledger
    AOP->>W: Publish(FundsUnlockRequestedEvent): ReleaseLock, a missing lock is a valid outcome
    Note over C,WOP: FundsLockRejectedEvent only clears the pending bid - a bid becomes visible after ~3-9 s (two outbox polls)
